course: dictionary
lesson: 12532
title: Destination
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A destination is the place you are going to. When you travel, it is where the journey ends. «The bus showed its destination on the front: Oxford.» The sign tells you where the bus is going, so destination means the place it is heading to.
explain: A destination can also be a place many people like to visit. «Spain is a popular holiday destination.» Here the word does not mean the end of one trip. It means a place people choose to go on holiday.
explain: A destination can even mean the goal you aim for. «Her destination was to finish the race, so she trained every day.» She was not travelling anywhere. The word shows the end she wanted to reach.
fact: A destination is the place someone or something is going to or being sent to.
fact: «Destination» can mean a popular place to visit, such as a holiday town.
fact: «Destination» can also mean the end or aim of something, like a goal you want to reach.
fact: Useful phrases: reach your destination, final destination, holiday destination, arrive at the destination.
fact: In maths journey problems, the distance «to the destination» is what you add up or divide by the speed.
exercise: «After six hours on the train, we finally reached our destination.» What does destination mean here? | *The place the journey ends | A long rest stop | A type of train ticket | The engine of the train
exercise: «Spain is a popular holiday destination.» What does this mean? | A kind of holiday food | A place nobody is allowed to go | *A place many people like to visit on holiday | A car park by the sea
exercise: «The map showed the route, the stops and the destination.» Find and copy the one word that means the place you are going to. | *destination | stops | map | route
test: Lucy wants to arrive at her destination before dark. What is her destination? | The time of day | Her bedroom | *The place she is going to | The name of her bike
test: «Her destination was to finish the race, so she trained every day.» What does destination mean here? | A rest stop on the route | Her starting line | *Her goal, the end she wants to reach | A pair of running shoes
exam: «The bus driver checked the destination sign before setting off.» What does destination mean? | A place to eat lunch | A kind of road | The colour of the bus | *The place the bus is going to
